WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.600
- I'm amazed by people's abilities

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.600
to build companies or incredible art.

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.070
But for me to admire someone

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.950
that means they've done something

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.884
that really touched my soul.

00:00:14.884 --> 00:00:16.950
(beat drops)

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.133
You got your perspective.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.877
(electronic music)
(crowd cheering)

00:00:21.877 --> 00:00:22.710
I just want to be happy.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.980
Don't you want to be happy?

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.270
- Gary Vaynerchuk, hey, how's it going?

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.840
- It's going well, how are you?

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.440
- I'm doing good, Gary.
- Good.

00:00:34.397 --> 00:00:38.020
- So, Gary, this is a podcast recording

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.360
for the Mindvalley podcast.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.570
But, one of the things that
we do a little bit differently

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.190
is that we have a live
audience watching us.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:46.010
So we have about 170 people right now.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.560
It'll probably go up to about 300 people.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.410
And the audience, these are
Mindvalley's biggest fans

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.780
have been helping me come
up with questions for you.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.450
First, how's it going?

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.283
How are you doing?

00:00:56.283 --> 00:00:59.300
I know the world has
been so different lately.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.920
- I lean into gratitude and perspective

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.900
and accountability during these times.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.693
And that's it.

00:01:06.693 --> 00:01:08.253
That's all I can do.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.300
- Well, one thing I got
to say about you, Gary,

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.963
is that I love the positivity
that you bring on stage.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.140
So just a little backstory

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.950
but I remember about a year ago,

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.710
we were speaking on stage together in,

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.920
in Sharjah, near Dubai, right?

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.940
You opened the conference,
I closed the conference.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.500
But what really touched me,

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.140
is how when you got on
stage at that audience,

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.630
in Sharjah, you were able
to adapt your message,

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:41.460
adapt your style, to an Arab
audience so effortlessly.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.640
- Thank you for saying that.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.270
- And at the same time, I've
seen you speak in Vegas,

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.860
and it's a completely different GaryVee.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:50.300
This was at Tony Robbins'
Business Freedom Mastery Summit,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.974
way, way back.

00:01:51.974 --> 00:01:53.850
We've shared the stage several times,

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.710
but we've only met once, at a pizza joint,

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:00.010
in Summit series, many
years ago aboard a ship.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.470
But I just want to express my gratitude

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:03.730
for having you as a guest here.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:04.563
- Thank you for having me.

00:02:04.563 --> 00:02:06.830
- I've been watching you
for 10 years and amazed

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:08.140
at how you've grown.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.523
Now because of how,

00:02:12.087 --> 00:02:13.390
when you speak, Gary,

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:14.530
you just go on a roll.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.810
So I do not want to interrupt
you in unnecessary questions.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.370
I want to give you a space

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:22.080
to share your message
to our audience today.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.150
The people who are watching are mostly,

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.743
60% leaders, managers, entrepreneurs,

00:02:26.743 --> 00:02:29.550
and they are all here as part
of the Mindvalley community

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.268
because they love personal growth.

00:02:32.268 --> 00:02:36.253
And these 300 people showed
up live because they love you.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:38.963
- It's very sweet.

00:02:38.963 --> 00:02:40.020
I'm so excited to be here.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.020
Let's rock and roll.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.840
- So with everything happening
in the world right now,

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.863
what would be your
advice to entrepreneurs?

00:02:48.607 --> 00:02:50.580
- You know, I think it is going into...

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.240
You know what's funny, when I
just answered your question,

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.150
I realized if I organize...

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.220
this literally how I create content,

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.200
this crew will probably see
a video tonight at 7:30 PM,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.773
Eastern American time,

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.690
where the title at the
top is going to say,

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:09.000
go into your GAP during times like this.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.120
Because serendipitously, I
decided to answer you with,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.120
you know, with gratitude
accountability, and perspective.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:19.940
I ordered it differently,

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.440
but as you and I were talking

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.460
I reordered it into spelling the word GAP.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.980
So, I'm actually going to
make that a piece of content.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.580
Like I literally have
just decided right here,

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.800
serendipitous, never put
those words together.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.990
So, that's fun. And it's
an insight to how I think.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:37.330
Which is like, creativity, information,

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:40.360
being skilled at something,
it requires omnipresence.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.290
You know, you can go train,

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:44.300
like I can go train to be a skier,

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.460
but I'm not going to
be a world class skier.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.970
For me, entrepreneurship,

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:51.330
and really wisdom and
perspective, came natural to me.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.820
It's my natural state.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.820
So, you know, what do
I tell entrepreneurs?

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.720
I tell them, this is
what you signed up for.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.623
Like, to really go there.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:05.220
What I tell fellow entrepreneurs
is like, this is our time.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.680
Like when things are challenging,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.370
when they're difficult,

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.960
when they're not stable,

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.180
is exactly when entrepreneurs do well.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.350
A pure, a real entrepreneur,

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.490
I don't like using the word real,

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.340
but like, an entrepreneur,

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.500
not someone over the last
decade, when it got cooler,

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.840
decided they wanted to be one.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:24.943
But an entrepreneur,

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.410
it's like being a fish,
and now here's the water.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.450
Like to me, this is our time.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.193
This is when you have to navigate.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.900
This is all we know.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:40.530
Like, you've signed up for a world where

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:43.420
you have to react to
realities on a daily basis

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.080
and it's all on your
accountable shoulders.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.647
And then when they're

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.160
incapable of going there,

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.870
I deploy perspective and gratitude.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:56.420
I remind my friends, some
who've been struggling,

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.580
that if COVID started six weeks earlier,

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.830
Kobe Bryant would be alive.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:03.623
You know, you can decide
to look at all the bad.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:09.160
Go look at the traffic
deaths data around the world.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.980
You know, you start getting
into scary debates of,

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.983
were more people's lives saved
during this time than lost?

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.623
It's half glass full, half glass empty.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.660
You start getting into really interesting,

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:22.493
thoughtful places.

00:05:22.493 --> 00:05:25.770
And so for me, it's perspective.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:28.180
You know, I think about World War II.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.770
I think about the Black Plague.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:32.680
I think about so many genocides.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.420
I think about the people
and the millions of people

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:38.390
around the world that don't
have clean water every day.

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.880
Not when there's not COVID.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:44.430
I'm not capable of
dwelling because of GAP.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:47.470
You know, gratitude, accountability,

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:50.750
like what am I going to do
about it, and perspective.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.000
And so I'm, what do I say?

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.130
I say, we should be thankful

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.820
that we can even have this conversation,

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:57.510
health over everything.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:02.510
And let's, you know, let's move forward.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:04.540
- I love that GAP concept.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:07.150
So gratitude, we get gratitude.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.600
Tell us about accountability.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.970
- Accountability is tricky,

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.670
because people confuse accountability

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:15.690
with lack of compassion.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.340
And I don't see it that way.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:20.993
You know, I view accountability
as, what can I control?

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.900
And so, you know, when
things like this happen,

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.253
people blame.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:28.300
People want to blame China.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.810
People want to blame their own government.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:33.205
People want to blame their
boss, their spouse, the system.

00:06:33.205 --> 00:06:36.210
And oftentimes there's
validity in those things.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:39.240
The question becomes, what
are you going to do about it?

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:42.030
You know, you can go political
and talk about voting.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:43.010
You can talk about people

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:44.410
that are in really suppressed
places about leaving,

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:45.610
if they can.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:46.810
You know, some places
you can't even leave,

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:48.730
but leaving, if you can.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:50.260
You know, for me, it's accountability.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.190
What can I do?

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:53.200
You know, when a lot of our,

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.160
in a very small, not
as heady conversation,

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.139
when my company is in trouble,

00:06:59.139 --> 00:07:01.320
when COVID hits 'cause
clients are telling us

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.970
they're not going to pay,
they have to reduce scopes.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.540
You know, first I stopped paying myself.

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:09.970
Then I stop wasting money on dumb stuff.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.870
So I look at all our expenses.

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.900
Then, unfortunately,
the worst of the bunch.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.850
I have to let some people go,

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:18.890
so the whole company can pay its bills.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:20.220
You know, life.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:23.100
And so, I like accountability.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.670
I like, you know, what am
I going to do about it?

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:30.120
And I don't think it's fun
or healthy to feel helpless.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:33.220
And I think it leads
to a lot of bad things.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.020
That doesn't mean that
I don't have compassion

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:37.570
for people that are in
precarious positions.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:41.420
It's just that I think
it's very empowering

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.638
for people to try to hack

00:07:43.638 --> 00:07:45.673
to think, what are they going to do?

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:50.503
- Now, the final one
was perspective, the P.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:52.930
- We've already touched on that, which is,

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:55.150
I use perspective and gratitude a lot.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.980
My perspective leads to gratitude,

00:07:56.980 --> 00:07:59.183
you know?
- Ah hah, right.

00:07:59.183 --> 00:08:00.050
- It could be worse, right?

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:02.143
My perspective is it could be worse.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:06.370
- So then, as you went
through this disruptive period

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:08.550
what was some of the life lessons,

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:10.713
the big insights that you gained?

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:15.200
- I got affirmation from who I think I am.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:18.160
During ironically, oh
my God, today is 9/11.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.960
So 9/11 was the first major event

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.870
I had to navigate through, as a leader.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:25.200
I was a very young kid
in a family business.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.350
Then there was the
great recession in 2008.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:29.483
These are macro things.

00:08:29.483 --> 00:08:31.070
As an entrepreneur and
operator, every day,

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.320
you're dealing with micro things:

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.470
lawsuits, somebody's family's
issues, clients, employees...

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:40.733
But macro, 9/11. Great recession.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:43.790
But I always, in the back
of my mind, my friend,

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:44.640
knew one thing.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.490
9/11 I was a kid.

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:49.670
I had, you know, I had no expenses.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:51.853
The great recession, you know,

00:08:51.853 --> 00:08:54.860
the reality was I built
the business for my dad,

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:56.490
not for myself the first time.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:09:01.140
So, even in 2008, I really
didn't have a lot, you know?

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.930
I had an apartment, but
not a whole, whole lot.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.260
I didn't have kids yet.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.730
So I always knew in the back
of my mind that I got...

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.930
I was a great entrepreneur
and I was fearless

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.270
and I put everything on my back,

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:14.780
but I really didn't have a lot to lose.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.493
So I always wondered, what would happen?

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.730
Not what would, when the
next big thing happens,

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:23.240
this is me five years ago, four years ago,

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:24.420
three years ago...

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:28.700
When that happens, am I going
to be as good navigating

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.450
when I'm clearly losing things?

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:34.240
Money, leisure, you know, who knows what?

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.900
Status. Whatever it may be. Fun.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:40.020
And the biggest thing I learned is,

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.720
I'm built for this shit.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:42.750
I'm born for this.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:46.780
You know? I went right into
the place where I needed to be.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:49.140
I knew what my requirement
was as a leader.

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:52.140
So I got affirmation of
my intuition of who I am.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:53.930
And I think I'm a wartime general.

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:57.093
I think I'm at my best
when it's most adverse.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.740
And I think that's because I
grew up in adverse situations.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.220
So that was nice,

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.900
so that was something I've learned.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:07.733
I've learned that people are,

00:10:10.974 --> 00:10:15.240
I was affirmed my suspicion

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:17.333
that people were soft and entitled.

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:21.440
You know, this is where
I keep going back to GAP.

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:24.940
You know, like, people...

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:29.010
we're not entitled to
have everything come easy.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:31.410
I don't know why people think we are.

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:35.360
It's not part of the life journey.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.457
Like, look at history, you know?

00:10:38.457 --> 00:10:40.000
Bad things happen.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.870
And like, really, really
bad things happen.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:47.510
And I think people have
become too materialistic

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:49.160
and have gotten complicated

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:54.160
in their need for acknowledgement
from outside forces

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.950
based on commercial successes,

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:00.075
or what car they drive, status.

00:11:00.075 --> 00:11:02.950
We're a very deeply, globally, globally,

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:04.220
a very deeply

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:10.360
insecure animal.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:14.530
And we need other people's
opinions for validation.

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:18.360
And I wish people could get
validation from their process.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:21.520
Not from the things that their
process allows them to buy

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:23.790
to make them look good to others.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.290
So, you know,

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:29.003
I've learned some human
truths that were suspicions.

00:11:31.582 --> 00:11:36.582
And I also learned that

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:38.010
every situation's different.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:40.080
I'm speaking in generalities right now.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:41.180
There's 7 billion people.

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:42.500
Plenty of people have excelled.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.580
Plenty of people don't
need a BMW to look cool,

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:46.612
they just like how it drives.

00:11:46.612 --> 00:11:50.880
You know, more affirmation
around me knowing

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.040
that there are thematics
I'm passionate about,

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.500
and I'm sharing them now,

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.670
but every individual is different,

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.270
going through their own cycle.

00:11:57.270 --> 00:12:00.343
And I have a lot of compassion
and empathy for that.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:02.283
- That's amazing.

00:12:02.283 --> 00:12:03.116
That's beautiful.

00:12:03.116 --> 00:12:06.000
So the audience, we now
have 500 people live,

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.260
the audience has a series
of questions for you.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.310
Can we take some questions
from the audience, Gary?

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:11.143
- Of course.

00:12:11.143 --> 00:12:13.196
- So the first question
is from Jason Whalser.

00:12:13.196 --> 00:12:15.763
Do you still believe in the hustle?

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:17.900
- Absolutely.

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:22.640
Now, I think the word, when
I used it in 2009 a lot,

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:25.400
meant hard work.
- Mm hmm.

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:28.250
- I think the word has
been manipulated in society

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:32.203
in the last half decade to mean burnout.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:38.120
And so I've switched using
it, more in a world of like,

00:12:40.464 --> 00:12:42.700
you know, when a word changes its meaning

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.890
to a large group of people,
you have to acknowledge that.

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:47.630
So, I use the word work ethic a lot more.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:49.530
I will forever believe in work ethic.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:52.510
There's nothing accomplished
without the execution.

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:53.910
And I believe in work ethic.

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:59.770
Not to the expense of someone's
health or mental status,

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:01.470
but I'm a very, very big advocate.

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:04.150
I would argue that I believe
in work ethic more today

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:05.363
than I did a decade ago.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.470
- So if you have to break it down, right?

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:12.618
When you say work ethic, what
does that look like for you?

00:13:12.618 --> 00:13:14.870
Like, you know, how you
came up with that acronym

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.910
GAP, what's work ethic for you?

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:20.980
- It's like, we can all agree that there's

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.810
a certain amount of liquid
in this bucket, right?

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:26.254
- Uh huh
- To me that's work ethic.

00:13:26.254 --> 00:13:29.110
Like, everyone in here and,

00:13:29.110 --> 00:13:31.670
reading these incredible
comments, observations, questions,

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:35.890
everybody in here is
got different skill sets

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:36.980
in different things.

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:40.095
So if I put in seven hours a
day into learning how to cook,

00:13:40.095 --> 00:13:42.530
over time, I could be a
much, much better cook,

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:45.910
but I may not be as great as Jason Holzer

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:47.340
or Jan McKinney or Anna.

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.860
Cause they just actually had talent

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.280
along with their work ethics.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.200
So there is a talent, work ethic thing.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:54.850
But, it takes an enormous amount

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:56.800
of work to be Beyonce or LeBron.

00:13:56.800 --> 00:14:00.937
And/or, probably every
single person, here, right?

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:06.050
Every one of us are
going to really struggle

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:09.490
to not recognize that the
hours put into our craft,

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.750
our execution, the time
you put into your children,

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:14.160
your employees, making this,

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.270
trying to figure out the formula for this.

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:18.480
Like, you know, for me, it's listening.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:19.760
I spend so much time listening.

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:21.440
You know, everybody sees
me talking all the time,

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:23.100
but I spend 90% of my time listening.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:26.281
It's why I have early
observations on things.

00:14:26.281 --> 00:14:27.930
And so, I work at that.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:30.240
